## What Is Real Estate Performance Management?

- [AppFolio Performance Platform](https://www.appfolio.com/performance-platform): The AppFolio Performance Platform is AppFolio's unified system for Real Estate Performance Management. It combines an AI-native data architecture, a System of Record, a System of Action, a System of Growth, and a Unified Experience — all accessible from a single login.
- [Real Estate Performance Management Explained] (https://www.appfolio.com/rpm/what-is-rpm): What is RPM? RPM is a new operating model that helps you shift from a reactive mode of property management towards a proactive, outcome-oriented approach. Learn About Real Estate Performance Management.
- [Real Estate Performance Management](https://www.appfolio.com/innovations): Real Estate Performance Management (RPM) is the discipline of developing competitive advantage by creating and sustaining a mutual exchange of value for all stakeholders in a real estate ecosystem — residents, property managers, investors, and vendors. RPM replaces task-based, reactive property management with proactive, outcome-oriented operations.
- [The Performance Gap](https://www.appfolio.com/blog/performance-gap): The Performance Gap is the space between what a real estate business needs to achieve and what its systems and teams are actually built to deliver. It is caused by task-based property management, fragmented technology, bolted-on AI, and a lack of unified visibility across the portfolio.
- [How a Unified Tech Experience Closes the Performance Gap](https://www.appfolio.com/blog/unified-tech-experiece): Beyond Features: Learn How a Unified Tech Experience Closes the Performance Gap. A unified tech experience is about delivering consistency, clarity, and performance across your entire organization, for your team, your residents, and your investors.


